#!/usr/bin/env bash
#USAGE: help — list the ./c commands

set -euo pipefail

cat <<'USAGE'
./c — The Hack Collective commands (hackcollective.uk and work.hackcollective.uk)

  ./c up [site|work] [mock-data:empty|mock-data:full]
                         start the dev servers in the background: site on :5173, work on :5281.
                         Runs under op run --environment (the 1Password dev Environment id is in
                         scripts/c/_lib/op-environments.sh). No .env or .dev.vars file.
                         With no Clerk keys, the work app opens signed in.
  ./c status             which dev servers run, where, and for how long
  ./c quit [site|work]   stop the dev servers that ./c up started
  ./c doctor             is this checkout set up the way the repo says?

  ./c check [step …]     the one gate: lockfile, structure, syntax, styles, deps, types, format,
                         cycles, clones, dead-code, health, schema. ./c check --list shows each step.
  ./c pre-commit         the commit gate (scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit runs it): ./c check --staged
  ./c verify [--staged|--diff SHA]
                         the fast check of what changed while you edit
  ./c explain <rule-id>  the message, reason, files and fix of one rule
  ./c align [path…]      measure alignment, spacing and hit areas of a running page
  ./c hooks              point git at scripts/git-hooks (pre-commit and pre-push)
  ./c review <PR>        adversarial Opus review of a PR head, posted with its P1 count
  ./c merge <PR>         squash-merge a PR when ./c review found no P1 and the rules hold (the only way into main)

Production ships through Workers Builds on a merge to main. Do not deploy by hand.
USAGE
